hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18526","Isma'il narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his brother Mutarrif, from Iyad ibn Himar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever picks up a lost item, let him call to witness a just person or two just persons, then let him neither conceal nor hide it, then if its owner comes, he is most entitled to it, otherwise it is the wealth of Allah which He gives to whom He wills."
"18527","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah, from Iyad ibn Himar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The sin of two persons insulting each other for what they both said is upon the one who began, so long as the wronged one does not transgress. And two persons insulting each other are two devils lying against each other and vilifying each other."
"18528","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Iyad ibn Himar al-Mujashi'i, he raised the hadith, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah Almighty commanded me to teach you what you were ignorant of from what He taught me this day of mine, and He said: Every wealth I have granted My servants is lawful for them. Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Hisham from Qatadah, and said: And the people of the Fire are five: the weak one who has no sense, those among you who are followers seeking neither family nor wealth."
"18529","Rawh narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Hakim al-Athram, from al-Hasan, he said: Mutarrif ibn Abdullah narrated to me, Iyad ibn Himar al-Mujashi'i narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in a sermon he delivered: Allah Almighty commanded me to teach you what you were ignorant of from what He taught me this day of mine. He said: And every wealth I have granted My servants is lawful for them. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"18530","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Ziyad al-Adawi narrated to us, and Yazid the brother of Mutarrif narrated to me, he said: And Uqbah narrated to me, all of these say: Mutarrif narrated to me, that Iyad ibn Himar narrated to him, that he heard the Prophet say in his sermon: Allah Almighty commanded me to teach you what you were ignorant of. Then he mentioned the hadith, and said: The weak one who has no sense, those among you who are followers seeking neither family nor wealth. He said: A man said to Mutarrif: O Abu Abdullah, is he from the clients or from the Arabs. He said: He is the follower who belongs to a man, acquiring from his servants through fornication without marriage. And he said: The people of Paradise are three: a just, truthful, certain ruler, and a merciful man tender-hearted toward every relative and Muslim, and a chaste poor man who gives charity. Hammam said: One of the companions of Qatadah said, and I know it only as Yunus al-Iskaf, he said to me: Qatadah did not hear the hadith of Iyad ibn Himar from Mutarrif. I said: He narrated to us from Mutarrif, and you say he did not hear it from Mutarrif. He said: A bedouin came and began asking him and was bold with him. He said: We said to the bedouin: Ask him whether he heard the hadith of Iyad ibn Himar from Mutarrif. So he asked him, and he said: No, four narrated to me from Mutarrif, then he named three of whom I told you."
"18531","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Yazid the brother of Mutarrif, from Iyad ibn Himar, that the Prophet said: The sin of two persons insulting each other for what they both said is upon the one who began, until the wronged one retaliates, or so long as the wronged one does not retaliate."
"18532","Affan narrated to us, Hammam with this chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah said: Two persons insulting each other are two devils lying against each other and vilifying each other."
"18533","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Khalid narrate from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Iyad ibn Himar, from the Prophet that he said: Whoever picks up a lost item, let him call to witness two just persons or one just person, Khalid is the doubter, and let him neither conceal nor hide it, then if its owner comes, he is most entitled to it, otherwise it is the wealth of Allah which He gives to whom He wills."
"18534","He said: I heard Yahya ibn Sa'id say: Mutarrif is twenty years older than al-Hasan, and Abu al-Ala is ten years older than al-Hasan. A brother of Abu Bakr ibn al-Aswad narrated it to me, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abu Aqil al-Dawraqi, with this."
